  <!-- ═══ PRIVACY POLICY PAGE ═══ -->
  <div class="page" id="page-privacy">
    <div class="legal-page">
      <div class="legal-back">
        <button class="article-back-btn" onclick="showPage('home')">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><line x1="19" y1="12" x2="5" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 19 5 12 12 5"/></svg>
          <span>Back</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-header">
        <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: July 4, 2026</p>
      </div>
      <div class="legal-body">

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>1. Overview</h2>
          <p>Friends Remover ("the Extension", "we", "us", or "our") is a browser extension that helps you manage your Roblox friends list. This Privacy Policy explains what data the Extension accesses, how it is used, how long it is retained, whether it is shared with any third party, and what rights you have over that data.</p>
          <p>By installing or using Friends Remover, you agree to the practices described in this policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2. Data We Access</h2>
          <p>The Extension accesses the following data in order to function:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Roblox session cookie (.ROBLOSECURITY):</strong> Read-only access is used solely to verify that you are logged in to Roblox and to authenticate API requests to Roblox on your behalf. The cookie value is never copied, stored outside your browser, or sent to any server other than Roblox's own.</li>
            <li><strong>Roblox friends list:</strong> Fetched directly from the Roblox API within your browser session to display your friends and allow you to select which to remove. This list is held in memory only and discarded when you close the extension popup.</li>
            <li><strong>Roblox user identity (user ID and username):</strong> Retrieved from the Roblox API to confirm which account is active. Your Roblox user ID is used as a key to store and retrieve your data on our cloud worker (see Section 3).</li>
            <li><strong>Active browser tab URL (roblox.com tabs only):</strong> The extension inspects whether a roblox.com tab is open in order to relay authenticated API requests. Tab content or browsing history is never read or recorded.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Separately, if you choose to submit the optional uninstall feedback survey on this website, we collect the data described in Section 2A below.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2A. Uninstall Feedback Survey (Website)</h2>
          <p>When you uninstall the Extension, you may be shown an optional feedback page on this website. If you submit that form, we collect:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Your survey responses:</strong> The reason(s) you selected for uninstalling and any free-text feedback you choose to type. Please avoid including personal information (such as your name or email address) in free-text fields, as we cannot control what you enter.</li>
            <li><strong>Browser and device information:</strong> Your browser name (e.g. Chrome, Firefox), whether you are on a mobile device, your general operating system/platform, and your browser's user-agent string. This helps us diagnose browser-specific bugs.</li>
            <li><strong>Approximate country/region:</strong> Derived either from Cloudflare's network-level geolocation of your request, or, as a fallback, from your public IP address via a third-party geolocation lookup (see Section 8). We only receive a country name/code — not a precise location.</li>
            <li><strong>A one-way hash of your IP address:</strong> Your raw IP address is not stored. It is cryptographically hashed and the hash is used only to apply a short cooldown between submissions and to prevent spam/abuse of the feedback form. The hash cannot practically be reversed to reveal your original IP address.</li>
            <li><strong>Extension version:</strong> The version of the Extension you had installed, to help us identify version-specific issues.</li>
            <li><strong>Optional diagnostic telemetry:</strong> When available, aggregate counts and stable types of error messages shown by the Extension, plus normalized API endpoints that failed, HTTP/network status, failure reason, and occurrence count. We do not include request bodies, cookies, query strings, or raw account-specific IDs in this diagnostic summary. A short recent console preview may also be attached to help reproduce bugs.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Submitting this survey is entirely optional and is not required to uninstall the Extension.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2B. Third-Party Services Used to Process Feedback</h2>
          <p>Submitted feedback is processed using the following third-party services, acting as data processors on our behalf:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare Workers:</strong> Hosts the backend that receives, stores, and relays feedback submissions. See Section 3.</li>
            <li><strong>Groq:</strong> Automatically screens free-text feedback content for spam or abusive submissions before a report is finalized. Feedback text is sent to Groq's API for this classification only.</li>
            <li><strong>Brevo:</strong> Used to email a copy of certain feedback reports to our internal team. See <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Brevo's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Discord:</strong> A summary of feedback reports may be posted to a private Discord channel via a webhook, for internal review by our team. See <a href="https://discord.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>IP geolocation providers (ipapi.co, ipwho.is, freeipapi.com):</strong> Used as a fallback to determine your approximate country when Cloudflare's own geolocation is unavailable. Your IP address is sent to whichever of these services responds first; we only retain the resulting country name/code, not the IP address itself or any response from these providers beyond that.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2C. Retention of Feedback Data</h2>
          <p>Feedback reports (including survey responses, browser/country metadata, and the hashed IP cooldown record) are retained for up to 30 days on our cloud worker before automatic deletion. Hashed-IP abuse-prevention records may be retained for up to 90 days. Copies sent via email or Discord for internal review are retained according to those platforms' own retention settings and our internal review process.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2D. In-Extension Bug Reports</h2>
          <p>The Extension includes an optional bug-report form accessible from the popup. If you choose to submit a report, we collect and transmit:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Your report text:</strong> The description you type. Please avoid including sensitive personal information in free-text fields.</li>
            <li><strong>Debug metadata:</strong> Your Extension version, browser version, and logged-in Roblox user ID, attached automatically to help us diagnose the issue.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>This data is sent over HTTPS to our reports server (<code>fmreports.zapgloob.workers.dev</code>), operated by the Extension developer. Submitting a bug report is entirely optional.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>2E. FR+ Membership Activation</h2>
          <p>If you purchase or activate FR+ (the Extension's premium membership, available via Roblox Subscription or Game Pass), the following data may be sent to our FR+ server (<code>frplus.faydynroblox.workers.dev</code>):</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Roblox user ID:</strong> Used to verify your Roblox game pass or subscription ownership and to register your membership record on our server.</li>
            <li><strong>Email address:</strong> If you use the optional email-verification step during FR+ activation, your email address is sent to our FR+ server solely to deliver a one-time verification code. It is not used for marketing or retained beyond the verification flow.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>All payments are processed exclusively by Roblox. The Extension does not handle or store any payment card or billing information.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>3. Data Stored in the Cloud</h2>
          <p>To ensure your data persists across extension updates, reinstalls, and different devices, Friends Remover saves certain data to <strong>Cloudflare Workers</strong> — third-party cloud services operated on our behalf. This data is stored remotely and is keyed to your Roblox user ID. The following data is saved to the cloud:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Removal history:</strong> A record of Roblox friends you have removed using the extension, including their user IDs and the timestamp of removal. This lets you review your removal history even after updating or reinstalling the extension.</li>
            <li><strong>Extension settings:</strong> Your configured preferences such as removal speed/delay, notification settings, and other in-extension configuration values. Saving these remotely means your settings are restored automatically after any extension update.</li>
            <li><strong>Pinned friends:</strong> The list of Roblox friends you have pinned within the extension so they are protected from bulk removal. This list is synced to the cloud so your pins are not lost when the extension updates.</li>
            <li><strong>Auth Lock credentials (if enabled):</strong> If you choose to enable the optional Auth Lock feature, the credentials you configure are stored server-side only on our Cloudflare Worker. They are never written to your browser's local storage.</li>
            <li><strong>FR+ membership record (if applicable):</strong> If you have an active FR+ membership, a record linked to your Roblox user ID is stored on our FR+ server to confirm your membership status across devices.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>This data is transmitted over HTTPS and is associated with your Roblox user ID. It is not linked to your real name or any other personally identifying information beyond your Roblox account identity. All requests to our cloud workers are authenticated with HMAC-SHA-256 signatures so only you can access your data. The workers are operated solely to provide these features and the data is not used for any other purpose.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>4. Data Stored Locally on Your Device</h2>
          <p>In addition to cloud storage, the Extension also stores some data <strong>locally in your browser</strong> using the <code>chrome.storage</code> API and <code>localStorage</code>:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>User preferences:</strong> Your chosen color theme (e.g., light, dark, blue) and language setting.</li>
            <li><strong>Dismissed notification flags:</strong> Records of which in-extension notifications you have dismissed, so they are not shown again.</li>
            <li><strong>Cached cloud data:</strong> A local copy of your settings, removal history, and pinned friends fetched from the cloud worker, used to display your data while offline or between syncs.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Local data can be cleared at any time by removing the extension or clearing your browser's extension storage.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>5. Data We Do NOT Collect</h2>
          <p>The Extension itself does <strong>not</strong> collect, transmit, or store any of the following:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your name, email address, or any contact information</li>
            <li>Your Roblox password or authentication credentials</li>
            <li>Your full live Roblox friends list on any external server</li>
            <li>Browsing history, visited URLs, or tab content outside roblox.com</li>
            <li>Crash reports, usage analytics, or behavioural telemetry from within the Extension itself</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The friends-removed counter shown on this website is an aggregate figure derived from synced removal history across users and does <strong>not</strong> expose any individual user's data publicly.</p>
          <p><strong>Note:</strong> the optional uninstall feedback survey on this website (Section 2A) is a separate, opt-in flow. If you submit it, we collect limited browser/device metadata, an approximate country, and a hashed (non-reversible) form of your IP address, as described above. We do not collect this data through the Extension itself, and we do not collect your raw/unhashed IP address, precise location, or any device identifiers beyond what is listed in Section 2A.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>6. How Data Is Used</h2>
          <p>Data accessed by the Extension is used exclusively to provide core functionality: reading your Roblox friends list, performing removal actions on your behalf, and persisting your settings, removal history, and pinned friends across extension updates. Uninstall survey data (Section 2A) is used solely to understand why users uninstall and to fix bugs. No data is used for advertising, profiling, sale, or any purpose beyond what is described in this policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>7. Data Retention</h2>
          <p>Session data (live friends list, user identity) is held in memory only for the duration of an active popup session and is discarded when you close the popup.</p>
          <p>Cloud-stored data (removal history, settings, pinned friends) is retained for as long as you use the extension. You may request deletion of your cloud data at any time by contacting us (see Section 13). Local browser storage persists until you uninstall the extension or clear your browser's extension storage.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>8. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
          <p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your data. The following is a complete list of all parties with whom data is shared:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare Workers (fmstoragekv.zaggloob.workers.dev):</strong> Stores your removal history, extension settings, pinned friends, and (if enabled) Auth Lock credentials on our behalf. Cloudflare's infrastructure is used only as a data store; your data is not shared with Cloudflare for their own purposes beyond standard hosting. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>FR+ Server (frplus.faydynroblox.workers.dev):</strong> Operated by the Extension developer. Receives your Roblox user ID to verify and register FR+ membership. If you use the email-verification step during activation, your email address is also sent solely to deliver a one-time code.</li>
            <li><strong>Reports Server (fmreports.zapgloob.workers.dev):</strong> Operated by the Extension developer. Receives your voluntary bug-report text, Extension version, browser version, and Roblox user ID only when you explicitly submit a report via the in-extension form.</li>
            <li><strong>Roblox (roblox.com / rbxcdn.com):</strong> The Extension communicates with Roblox's APIs to read your friends list, verify login status, check game pass or subscription ownership, and perform friend-removal actions. All such requests are authenticated by your existing Roblox browser session. See <a href="https://en.help.roblox.com/hc/en-us/articles/115004630823" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Roblox's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Fonts (fonts.googleapis.com / fonts.gstatic.com):</strong> The Extension UI and this website load the Inter typeface from Google's font CDN. Your IP address is transmitted as part of the standard font request. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>GitHub (raw.githubusercontent.com / api.github.com):</strong> The Extension fetches certain remote assets (e.g. logo image) and this website fetches blog content from GitHub. Your IP address is transmitted as a standard HTTP header; no account data is sent. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub's Privacy Statement</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>Groq, Brevo, Discord, and IP geolocation providers (ipapi.co, ipwho.is, freeipapi.com):</strong> Used only when you submit the optional uninstall feedback survey on this website. See Section 2B for details.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>No other third-party analytics, advertising networks, pixels, or tracking scripts receive your data from the Extension or this website.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>9. Security</h2>
          <p>All data transmitted between the Extension and our Cloudflare Worker is encrypted in transit via HTTPS. Access to your cloud-stored data is scoped to your Roblox user ID and is protected by HMAC-signed requests. Your Roblox session cookie is handled exclusively by your browser and is never copied by the extension or sent to our worker.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>Friends Remover is designed for general use by Roblox users. It is not directed at children under the age of 13 (or the applicable age of digital consent in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect any personal information from children. If you believe a child's data has been stored through the extension, please contact us and we will take appropriate steps to delete it.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>11. Your Rights</h2>
          <p>You have the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of the data we hold about you on our cloud worker (removal history, settings, pinned friends), as well as any uninstall feedback survey submission (Section 2A) associated with information you provide us. To exercise these rights, contact us using the details in Section 13. All locally stored extension data can be deleted at any time by uninstalling the extension or clearing your browser's storage for the extension.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in the Extension's features or applicable law. Updates will be reflected by a revised "Last updated" date at the top of this page. Continued use of the Extension after any update constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
          <h2>13. Contact</h2>
          <p>If you have any questions, concerns, or requests regarding this Privacy Policy or your data, you can reach us at <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#37545859435654437751455e5259534445525a584152451954585a"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="fd9e9293899c9e89bd9b8f949893998e8f9890928b988fd39e9290">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> or via our <a href="https://discord.gg/Z3Vqjb7SZc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord server</a>.</p>
        </section>

      </div>
